 { Aside from time trouble, there are only three causes of calculation mistakes: 1. Dismissing Tactical Motifs 2. Unfamiliarity with Patterns 3. Poor Visualisation These causes can be extremely costly. In this chapter, I will show some examples of miscalculations in action. At the end, I will wrap up the entire course with a summary of what you could do to further develop your chess calculation skill. }  
 *

[Event "Calculation: A Complete Guide for Tournament Players"]
[Site "https://www.chessable.com/variation/12046108/"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "7.2"]
[White "6. Typical Mistakes"]
[Black "Dismissing Tactical Motifs"]
[Result "*"]

 { It can be very easy to dismiss an unprotected piece or a trappable piece simply because it seems irrelevant. However, by doing so, we are ignoring crucial hints that will reveal which moves you should be looking at. For the next few puzzles, you can expect much more obscure tactical motifs. So be sure to follow through the Burger Technique like you have done since the beginning of the course. Remember, never be too quick to dismiss a tactical motif. }  
 *

