[FEN "r1b1k2r/pp1nqpp1/4p2p/3pP1N1/8/3BQ3/PP3PPP/2R2RK1 w kq - 0 1"]

 { You may recognise this game between Magnus Carlsen (White) and Tor Gulbrandsen Ostlandserien (Black) . What did young Carlsen do about his attacked g5 Knight? } 1. { -KEY- } Qxa7 $3 { This was why Carlsen put his Rook on c1 a move ago! He knew that the seemingly irrelevant unprotected c8 Bishop would cause big trouble for Black. } Rxa7 2. Rxc8+ Qd8 3. Rxd8+ Kxd8 4. Nxf7+ Ke7 5. Nxh8 { Carlsen can use the g6 escape square for his Knight and he will enjoy a healthy material advantage. } 
