 { Remember to establish the tactical motifs before considering candidate moves } 1... { -KEY- } Nc3 { Both of White's Bishops are unprotected and the b4 Queen is trappable. This move hits the e2 Bishop while sealing off the b4 Queen's escape route. Black has a strong threat of ...Rb8 } 2. Bb5 { Shielding the Queen from ...Rb8 } Rb8 { Pinning the Bishop and forcing a4 } 3. a4 Ne2+ { Now that the light-squared Bishop is pinned, Black can go for this fork } 4. Kh1 Nxc1 { Black can use the b3 escape square for his Knight. } 
