 { As I have emphasised in Chapters 3 and 4, you should never underestimate the power of patterns in chess. Recognising patterns in a complex position is like wearing night vision goggles to a pitch black battle arena. You will be able to see so much more than your opponent. Therefore, when you are unable to solve a puzzle despite conscientiously executing the Burger Technique, it is quite likely that you are just not familiar with the patterns or the precursors to tactics. The subsequent puzzles contain patterns that have caught my students off-guard before. Don’t worry if you can’t solve them, simply think of it as a chess lesson on a fresh pattern and execute PIE. }  
 *

[Event "Calculation: A Complete Guide for Tournament Players"]
