 { This is taken from one of my casual blindfold rapid games. What is White's best plan? } 1. { -KEY- } Kb1 $1 { White does not have to concede to the Black Queen's perpetual check. But how does White save the Knight and Rook after the fork } Qd2 { Attacking e1 and e2 } 2. Qc1 $3 { Defending e1, and continuing to indirectly defend e2. Qc3 works too, but I didn't want to scare my opponent with the possibility of Qxf6+ } Rxe2 $2 3. Qc8+ Kg7 4. Qg4+ Kh8 5. Qxe2 { The Queen has just teleported from c1 to e2. Applying PIE here, you should have a deeper appreciation of the dangers of an exposed King } 
